WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.510
Here on the show we love

2
00:00:01.510 --> 00:00:02.958
to shine a light on people,

3
00:00:02.958 --> 00:00:05.830
who are working hard to help other people.

4
00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:09.570
And today we have got this incredible story

5
00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:11.560
of three cancer survivors.

6
00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:14.580
And Gail's friend and CBS news colleague,

7
00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:19.045
David Begnaud went out and filed this Drew-Gooder report.

8
00:00:19.045 --> 00:00:21.428
(upbeat music begins)

9
00:00:21.428 --> 00:00:23.279
(upbeat music fading)

10
00:00:23.279 --> 00:00:24.660
Hi, I'm Kerry.

11
00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:25.730
Hi, I'm Shelly.

12
00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:27.033
Hi, I'm Katy.

13
00:00:27.033 --> 00:00:29.200
[Kerry, Shelly, And Katy] And we're the cancer cartel.

14
00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:30.210
I was diagnosed

15
00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:32.173
with stage four non-Hodgkin's lymphoma.

16
00:00:32.173 --> 00:00:34.643
I was diagnosed with breast cancer.

17
00:00:34.643 --> 00:00:37.570
I battled breast cancer, thyroid cancer

18
00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.650
and I've had an ongoing battle with skin cancer.

19
00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:41.900
Kerry and I have been friends for about,

20
00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:43.370
I would say five years now.

21
00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:44.870
And me and Shelly are sisters.

22
00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:46.260
Katy and I were talking about

23
00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:48.040
how lucky we are to have made it

24
00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:50.119
through our cancer journeys that we were meant

25
00:00:50.119 --> 00:00:53.680
for more and the cancer cartel was formed.

26
00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:55.840
We accept luxury donated items

27
00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:57.308
or dollars on our website.

28
00:00:57.308 --> 00:01:00.790
We sell it and a hundred percent of the proceeds go directly

29
00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:02.780
into the hands of people fighting cancer.

30
00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:05.336
We're going to send you a check in the mail today.

31
00:01:05.336 --> 00:01:07.536
[Donation Recipient] Oh my gosh! Thank you so much!

32
00:01:07.536 --> 00:01:09.410
[Donation Recipient 2] Oh my God! You guys are awesome,

33
00:01:09.410 --> 00:01:10.243
Thank you so much!

34
00:01:10.243 --> 00:01:12.920
[Donation Recipient 3] I'm really grateful, I really am.

35
00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:14.900
I feel like I'm doing what I'm meant

36
00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:16.350
to do with people.

37
00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:17.780
I meant to do it with

38
00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:20.680
and that there's nothing that can stop us on this journey.

39
00:01:22.884 --> 00:01:25.467
(upbeat music)

40
00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:28.340
Hey, Drew, it's David Begnaud

41
00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:29.480
with CBS news.

42
00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:31.598
I am on a very special assignment here

43
00:01:31.598 --> 00:01:35.581
in Seattle to surprise Kerry, Katy and Shelly.

44
00:01:35.581 --> 00:01:37.660
(door knocking)

45
00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:38.754
Hello!

46
00:01:38.754 --> 00:01:40.420
(group greeting)

47
00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:42.910
Drew wanted me to surprise you guys

48
00:01:42.910 --> 00:01:44.369
with this.

49
00:01:44.369 --> 00:01:46.918
This is amazing! Are you kidding?

50
00:01:46.918 --> 00:01:49.626
(group cheering)

51
00:01:49.626 --> 00:01:51.890
(group cheering)

52
00:01:51.890 --> 00:01:52.880
You guys, you know what?

53
00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:54.730
We never get anything for ourselves.

54
00:01:54.730 --> 00:01:56.476
I'm going to start crying.

55
00:01:56.476 --> 00:01:57.647
No, we don't.

56
00:01:57.647 --> 00:01:58.720
"Drew Gooder"

57
00:01:58.720 --> 00:01:59.630
That's awesome.

58
00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:00.730
Oh my gosh!

59
00:02:02.486 --> 00:02:03.648
Thank you Drew!

60
00:02:03.648 --> 00:02:04.481
Thank you so much!

61
00:02:04.481 --> 00:02:05.314
Oh my gosh! We're blown away

62
00:02:05.314 --> 00:02:06.147
I don't really, I don't even know.

63
00:02:06.147 --> 00:02:08.700
I have no words.

64
00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:10.330
Coming here to surprise you guys

65
00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:11.390
on behalf of Drew.

66
00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:12.223
Incredible

67
00:02:12.223 --> 00:02:13.440
was so exciting for me.

68
00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:15.787
Like this is personal because my mother had breast cancer.

69
00:02:15.787 --> 00:02:16.930
[Kerry, Shelly, And Katy] Oh!

70
00:02:16.930 --> 00:02:19.400
And so I got really emotional

71
00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:21.660
watching what you all are doing

72
00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:23.530
for other people to pay it forward.

73
00:02:23.530 --> 00:02:25.730
We all have stories, but we shouldn't be here.

74
00:02:25.730 --> 00:02:29.030
And it was meant to be that we were supposed to be

75
00:02:29.030 --> 00:02:30.220
on this path together.

76
00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:31.210
I always had the back of my mind.

77
00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:33.170
I want to do something to give back, but I just

78
00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:36.030
didn't know what that thing was until these two.

79
00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:38.530
How does it feel to be recognized?

80
00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:39.552
It feels..

81
00:02:39.552 --> 00:02:40.780
[Kerry And Shelly] Surreal.

82
00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:43.421
People have been so amazing coming

83
00:02:43.421 --> 00:02:45.713
on board and support.

84
00:02:47.546 --> 00:02:48.900
I mean, y'all are the Drew Gooders

85
00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:50.944
that make the world a special place.

86
00:02:50.944 --> 00:02:53.778
Thank you so much!

87
00:02:53.778 --> 00:02:54.611
(crowd clapping)

88
00:02:54.611 --> 00:02:56.180
[Drew} Joining us now, CBS

89
00:02:56.180 --> 00:03:00.168
this morning lead national correspondent, David Begnaud!

90
00:03:00.168 --> 00:03:03.572
(crowd cheering)

91
00:03:03.572 --> 00:03:05.930
I really wanna compliment you because

92
00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:07.865
sometimes when you see these pieces

93
00:03:07.865 --> 00:03:09.600
you feel like it's all wrapped up

94
00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:12.960
in a bow and it just makes you feel really good.

95
00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:15.160
This is not only a feel-good story

96
00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:16.950
but it's very incentivizing.

97
00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:19.070
I want to do more with these women.

98
00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:21.980
And I hope that other people feel that too, watching it.

99
00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:25.380
I think your journalistic style is just perfection

100
00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:26.890
because it's not like great.

101
00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:28.460
That's all happening and taken care of.

102
00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:29.470
I can move on with my life.

103
00:03:29.470 --> 00:03:30.303
It makes me go.

104
00:03:30.303 --> 00:03:31.402
I want to get involved.

105
00:03:31.402 --> 00:03:32.235
Well, first of all, thank you

106
00:03:32.235 --> 00:03:34.610
for allowing me to spread some joy on your behalf.

107
00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:37.360
And I have to tell you Drew those women between the three

108
00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:39.610
of them have had six different cancers almost right.

109
00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:41.880 line:15%
Six. So the gratitude they feel

110
00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:45.310 line:15%
for just being alive was palpable

111
00:03:45.310 --> 00:03:47.630 line:15%
and they were tickled pink that you thought enough

112
00:03:47.630 --> 00:03:50.090
about what they're doing to recognize them on your show.

113
00:03:50.090 --> 00:03:50.940
They were over the moon.

114
00:03:50.940 --> 00:03:51.773
It's not enough.

115
00:03:51.773 --> 00:03:53.040
I want to do more.

116
00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:54.500
You know, I've seen many different interviews

117
00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:55.333
with different people

118
00:03:55.333 --> 00:03:57.860
but there's something about when David does the interview.

119
00:03:57.860 --> 00:04:00.121
People open up to him in a way that they don't others.

120
00:04:00.121 --> 00:04:02.040
He really does have a special gift.

121
00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:04.530
So I'm not surprised you do you recognize that?

122
00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:05.780
I absolutely did.

123
00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:10.170
And out of curiosity, for all of us budding, you know

124
00:04:10.170 --> 00:04:12.904
lovers of journalism and the art of conversation

125
00:04:12.904 --> 00:04:13.980
Yeah

126
00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:17.390
how do you get all of this goodness out of people?

127
00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:18.460
I'll tell you what it is for me.

128
00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:20.435
Short soulful questions,

129
00:04:20.435 --> 00:04:23.010
this lady but there's nobody like her.

130
00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:24.920
Right? I adore her, but what I try

131
00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:27.580
and do is I go in and just be myself.

132
00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:29.170
And what I do Drew,

133
00:04:29.170 --> 00:04:30.890
is a lot of people are expecting big questions.

134
00:04:30.890 --> 00:04:31.723
They prep all night.

135
00:04:31.723 --> 00:04:33.130
They're like, he's gonna ask me the following.

136
00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:35.601
And I go in and I go, but why did you

137
00:04:35.601 --> 00:04:37.720
the moment you walked in

138
00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:40.520
or why didn't you say, and it's the simple

139
00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:43.740
short soulful that lead people to sort of go,

140
00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:45.700
well you want to know my heart.

141
00:04:45.700 --> 00:04:47.870
And when you can give me a piece of your heart

142
00:04:47.870 --> 00:04:49.530
that's where the audience is going to come back.

143
00:04:49.530 --> 00:04:50.800
All right, David, thank you,

144
00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:53.920
David and Gail catch Gail on CBS this morning

145
00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:56.210
and check out the new Oprah daily.

146
00:04:56.210 --> 00:04:58.430
I love that it has the word daily on there.

147
00:04:58.430 --> 00:04:59.263
We do too,

148
00:04:59.263 --> 00:05:01.310
and watch Oprah and Gail live tonight

149
00:05:01.310 --> 00:05:03.250
on zoom and go to our website

150
00:05:03.250 --> 00:05:05.840
for a special Oprah insider offered that

151
00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:07.310
by the way when I found out what it was,

152
